    "case_id": "99",
    "case_summary": "A woman in her 30s presented with progressive, multiple itchy erythematous to violaceous papules and plaques localized to the left shin for more than 10 years. On close inspection, milia and a few erosions with partially detached epidermis were identified. There were no abnormalities of the mucous membranes, nails, hair, or teeth. No extracutaneous involvement was observed.\n\nMultiple pruritic erythematous to violaceous lichenified papules and plaques on the left shin. Close-up examination revealed erosion with partially detached epidermis and multiple milia.\n\n- Histopathologic examination:    Image Title: Histopathologic examination with hematoxylin-eosin stain (Figure C)    Image Description: Revealed dermoepidermal separation        Image Title: Histopathologic examination with hematoxylin-eosin stain (Figure D)     Image Description: Revealed several milia in the superficial dermis  - Genetic Testing:    Whole-exome sequencing identified a novel heterozygous missense variant, c.6832G>T, p.Gly2278Trp, in COL7A1 (NM_000094)    Sanger sequencing confirmed cosegregation of this variant",
    "frontier": [
